## 2. Definitions

**"Licensor"** means Akshay V S, the individual or legal entity that makes the Software available under this License.

**"Software"** means the software, source code, object code, documentation, configuration files, and other materials distributed by the Licensor under this License.

**"You"** means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this License.

**"Organization"** means any company, corporation, partnership, sole proprietorship, nonprofit organization, governmental entity, institution, or other legal or commercial organization.

**"Affiliate"** means an entity that directly or indirectly controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with an Organization.

**"Control"** means ownership of more than fifty percent (50%) of the voting interests of an entity, the power to direct its management or policies, or equivalent control.

**"Small Organization"** means an Organization whose consolidated gross annual revenue, together with the consolidated gross annual revenue of its Affiliates, was less than **US$100,000** during its most recently completed fiscal year.

**"Enterprise Organization"** means an Organization that does not qualify as a Small Organization.

**"Commercial Use"** means use of the Software in connection with a business, commercial activity, revenue-generating activity, or the provision of goods or services.

**"Self-Hosted Deployment"** means a deployment of the Software operated by You or by a third party on Your behalf on infrastructure that is not directly operated and controlled by the Licensor as part of a service provided by the Licensor.

**"Hosted Service"** means a service in which the Software, or a modified or derivative version of the Software, is operated on behalf of one or more third parties and accessed remotely over a network, including through a web application, API, cloud service, managed service, or software-as-a-service offering.

**"Competing Product"** means any product or service whose primary purpose or material functionality is substantially similar to, substitutes for, or competes with the Software or any ecommerce product or service provided by the Licensor using the Software.

A Competing Product includes, without limitation, a hosted, cloud, managed, multi-tenant, white-label, or software-as-a-service ecommerce platform that provides functionality substantially similar to the Software or the Licensor's products or services.

A product or service may be a Competing Product regardless of:

- whether it is offered for payment or free of charge;
- whether it is hosted on the provider's infrastructure or a third party's infrastructure;
- whether it is modified from the Software;
- whether it incorporates the Software directly or indirectly;
- whether it uses a different user interface or technical architecture;
- whether it is written in a different programming language; or
- whether it is marketed under a different name or brand.

**"Enterprise License"** means a separate written commercial license or agreement issued by the Licensor that authorizes an Enterprise Organization to use the Software.

